<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · island</p><h1 class="enc-title">Hong Kong Island</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hong-kong">Hong Kong</a> Island is an island on the south side of Victoria Harbour, at the mouth of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pearl-river">Pearl River</a> in southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a>. Occupied by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a> in 1841 during the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-opium-war">First Opium War</a> and ceded by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-nanjing">Treaty of Nanjing</a> in 1842, it became the core of the colony of Hong Kong, with its capital at Victoria. It returned to Chinese <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sovereignty">sovereignty</a> with the rest of Hong Kong in 1997.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/hong-kong-island.jpg" alt="Hong Kong Island" width="320" height="161" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: momo from Hong Kong · CC BY 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Hong_Kong_Island_Skyline_201108.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
